*(Power Round, Problem 2.3)* Label the vertices of an equilateral triangle $1$ (top), $2$ (bottom left), $3$ (bottom right); this is the initial labelling $I$. Rotating the original triangle counterclockwise by $120^\circ$ gives the labelling $R_{120}$ with $3$ at the top, $1$ at the bottom left, $2$ at the bottom right; rotating by $240^\circ$ gives $R_{240}$ with $2$ at the top, $3$ at the bottom left, $1$ at the bottom right (see the figure). Flips: $F_A$ flips across the vertical perpendicular bisector, $F_B$ across the perpendicular bisector that bisects the right side, $F_C$ across the perpendicular bisector that bisects the left side. Compositions are written as functions: $T\circ S$ means do $S$ first, then $T$. For example $F_A\circ R_{120}=F_B$, $R_{120}\circ F_A=F_C$ and $R_{240}=F_B\circ F_A$. Below, a labelling is written (top, bottom left, bottom right).

Draw (describe) the resulting labelling of the triangle after each sequence of transformations applied to the original triangle:

(a) a $120^\circ$ counterclockwise rotation followed by a flip across the vertical perpendicular bisector;

(b) a flip across the vertical perpendicular bisector followed by a $120^\circ$ counterclockwise rotation;

(c) a $120^\circ$ counterclockwise rotation followed by a flip across the vertical perpendicular bisector followed by a $240^\circ$ counterclockwise rotation.
